# Trivy CVE allowlist. AGENTS.md policy: each entry needs a rationale + review-by date.
# When the upstream fix lands (or the review-by date arrives), audit and remove.

# CVE-2026-42570 (HIGH): devalue DoS via sparse array deserialization
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42570
# Affects: devalue 5.7.1 (via @astrojs/react 5.0.4) + devalue 5.8.0 (via astro 6.3.1)
# Fix: devalue 5.8.1
# Tried pnpm override `devalue: ^5.8.1` in pnpm-workspace.yaml; pnpm 11's
# minimumReleaseAge default (1440 min = 1 day) silently refused to apply the
# bump, leaving transitives pinned. Deferring via this allowlist instead.
# Review-by: 2026-08-15 (re-check after astro / @astrojs/react release a
# version that pulls devalue >= 5.8.1; drop this line when upstream bumps).
CVE-2026-42570

# GHSA-gv7w-rqvm-qjhr (HIGH): esbuild missing binary integrity verification in
# its Deno module enables RCE. https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gv7w-rqvm-qjhr
# Affects: esbuild 0.27.3 (via wrangler) + 0.27.7 (via astro / vite). Fix: 0.28.1.
# Not applicable here: the vulnerable code path is esbuild's Deno binary loader;
# this is a Node/pnpm project, so that path is never exercised. A pnpm override
# to 0.28.1 is also not viable (vite 7 pins esbuild < 0.28, and pnpm 11's
# minimumReleaseAge blocks the fresh release).
# Review-by: 2026-09-15 (drop once astro / vite / wrangler pull esbuild >= 0.28.1).
GHSA-gv7w-rqvm-qjhr

# CVE-2026-48779 (HIGH): ws memory-exhaustion DoS from tiny fragments + data chunks.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-48779
# Affects: ws 8.20.1 via the Cloudflare / wrangler dev tooling (dev-only; the
# production runtime is workerd, not ws). Fix: 8.21.0, already in the tree via
# happy-dom / vitest. A pnpm override to 8.21.0 is silently refused by pnpm 11's
# minimumReleaseAge (the release is < 1 day old), same as the devalue case above.
# Review-by: 2026-07-15 (re-try the override once the cooldown clears, or drop
# when the Cloudflare tooling bumps ws >= 8.21.0).
CVE-2026-48779

# CVE-2026-9697 (HIGH): undici man-in-the-middle via ignored TLS options when a
# SOCKS5 proxy is configured. https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9697
# Affects: undici 7.24.8, which miniflare 4.x pins EXACTLY (the Cloudflare dev
# tooling; dev-only, the production runtime is workerd, not undici). The
# vulnerable path needs undici wired to a SOCKS5 proxy, which the dev server
# never does. Fix: 7.28.0, already resolved elsewhere in the tree (via
# @semantic-release/github), but a pnpm override to dedupe miniflare onto it is
# silently ignored by pnpm 11 in both pnpm-workspace.yaml and
# package.json#pnpm.overrides (same refusal as the entries above), because
# miniflare hard-pins the exact 7.24.8.
# Review-by: 2026-08-15 (drop once miniflare / wrangler bump undici >= 7.28.0).
CVE-2026-9697
